I have to say, it actually disappointed me
when I got back in the Ferrari.

164
00:09:55,880 --> 00:09:57,160
克拉克森：确实。
- 啥动静都听不见了。
CLARKSON: It did.
- You couldn't hear anything.

165
00:09:57,200 --> 00:09:58,760
克拉克森：听着跟台
福特嘉年华似的。
CLARKSON: Well, it sounds
like a Ford Fiesta.

166
00:09:58,800 --> 00:10:00,760
但你要是有这长相，再配上这声浪，
But if you have those looks, and the noise,

167
00:10:00,800 --> 00:10:03,920
而且开着阿斯顿就有种魔力，
能让路人看着你都顺眼得多。
and there's something that makes people
like you more if you're in an Aston.

168
00:10:03,960 --> 00:10:05,960
我觉得你从辅路拐出来，
愿意给你让行的人
I think you would be allowed
out of more side turns

169
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:07,560
肯定比你开法拉利时多得多，
than you would if you had the Ferrari,

170
00:10:07,600 --> 00:10:09,360
开法拉利别人只会觉得你像个嘚瑟的舒马赫。
when you are a bit of a Schumacher.

171
00:10:09,400 --> 00:10:11,680
嗯，我们可不想被当成那样！
Hmm. We don't want that!

172
00:10:11,720 --> 00:10:12,680
[两人大笑]
[BOTH LAUGHING]

173
00:10:18,800 --> 00:10:21,000
理查德·哈蒙德：杰里米，
你刚才那段真就开了40英里时速？
RICHARD HAMMOND: Jeremy,
you were doing 40 miles an hour there?

174
00:10:21,040 --> 00:10:23,440
那必须的。在拍那部片子的
Absolutely. We never
exceeded the speed limit

175
00:10:23,480 --> 00:10:26,240
整个过程中，我们连一次超速都没有过。
once in the entire making
of that film there.

176
00:10:26,280 --> 00:10:30,480
不过不得不说，
对我而言那绝对是最美好的一天，
I have to say, though,
it was, for me, one of the greatest days,

177
00:10:30,520 --> 00:10:34,960
摸着良心讲。法拉利、
阿斯顿·马丁、阳光普照，还有戴蒙·希尔。
honestly and truthfully. Ferrari,
Aston Martin, sun shone, Damon Hill.

178
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:36,560
简直爽如升天。
It was just heaven.

179
00:10:36,600 --> 00:10:39,400
而且，更精彩刺激的是，
And, what made it particularly exciting

180
00:10:39,440 --> 00:10:43,560
怀特岛当地的广播电台“英明神武”地决定，
was that the local Isle of Wight
radio station decided, in its wisdom,

181
00:10:43,600 --> 00:10:45,040
直接在空中电波里大肆播报：
to broadcast the fact over the air that

182
00:10:45,080 --> 00:10:47,800
戴蒙和杰里米带着一台阿斯顿和一台法拉利来岛上了！
Damon and Jeremy were down there
with an Aston and a Ferrari.

183
00:10:47,840 --> 00:10:50,720
“大伙儿还不赶紧过去围观！”
"Why don't you all go along
and have a look?"

184
00:10:50,760 --> 00:10:53,000
于是我开着法拉利以“40码”过弯，
So I came around the corner,
at 40 in the Ferrari,

185
00:10:53,040 --> 00:10:55,240
就看见路边一个抹着大油头的家伙喊：
and there he is with his hair greased down,

186
00:10:55,280 --> 00:10:57,680
“我把我家的老虎窗带过来给你们瞧瞧。”我的天哪。
"I brought my dormer
down for you to have a look." Oh, God.

187
00:10:57,720 --> 00:10:59,320
[全场大笑]
[ALL LAUGHING]

188
00:10:59,360 --> 00:11:01,560
然后我们像赶羊一样把他们全轰下了路。爽翻了。
We then herded them
off the road. It was just heaven

189
00:11:01,600 --> 00:11:03,440
但你很喜欢这台车对吧？你很迷那台575。
But you loved this, didn't you?
You loved the 575.

190
00:11:03,480 --> 00:11:07,320
575是台绝妙无比的车，
但必须强调的是，
575 is a fabulous, fabulous car,
But it must be stressed,

191
00:11:07,360 --> 00:11:10,480
我在片子里开的那台装了费奥拉诺操控套件。
the one that I drove there had
the Fiorano Handling Pack on it.

192
00:11:10,520 --> 00:11:12,760
据说装上后整台车脱胎换骨。
Which transforms the car, apparently.

193
00:11:12,800 --> 00:11:16,160
原厂标配悬挂开着跟坐船似的，晃晃悠悠，偏软。
Standard suspension,
a bit wallow-y, a bit soft.

194
00:11:16,200 --> 00:11:18,120
但眼前这台配的可是阿斯顿那款箱子……
- 变速箱。
But this one was sporting the Aston box...
- Gearbox.

195
00:11:18,160 --> 00:11:19,600
那变速箱，说真的……
The gearbox, just, honestly...

196
00:11:19,640 --> 00:11:21,400
能有多烂？
[嗤笑] 彻底把整台车给毁了。
How bad was that?
[SCOFFS] It just ruins it.

197
00:11:21,440 --> 00:11:22,680
你甚至巴不得他们赶紧换掉它，
You just think just change it

198
00:11:22,720 --> 00:11:25,480
因为这玩意儿都严重拖累
二手车行情了。
'cause it's affecting
the second-hand values.

199
00:11:25,520 --> 00:11:28,920
可不是嘛。你要是揣着一巨笔钞票去买车，
Oh yeah. I mean, if you went out
with a slug of money,

200
00:11:28,960 --> 00:11:30,520
你恐怕很难说服自己买一台575。
you'd struggle to buy a 575.

201
00:11:30,560 --> 00:11:32,000
现在订那车得排多久的队？
What's the waiting list on that now?

202
00:11:32,040 --> 00:11:34,240
要是按原价提车的话，
差不多得等上个12到18个月。
Well, at list price,
it's kind of 12-18 months.

203
00:11:34,280 --> 00:11:36,080
真的假的？
- 克拉克森：真的。
Really?
- CLARKSON: Yeah.

204
00:11:36,120 --> 00:11:38,040
我的意思是，你要是肯加价，
倒是能早点提车。
I mean, if you want to pay a premium
you can get one before.

205
00:11:38,080 --> 00:11:39,080
但要是买Vanquish，我下周就能
原价给你弄来一台。
But with a Vanquish, I could get you one
next week list price.

206
00:11:39,120 --> 00:11:41,000
克拉克森：真的？
- 真的。
CLARKSON: Really?
- Yeah.

207
00:11:41,040 --> 00:11:43,120
至于二手车，虽然你看到广告上
挂的价格依旧坚挺，
And second-hand, whilst you will see them
advertised at strong money,

208
00:11:43,160 --> 00:11:45,600
但真要想拿去置换脱手，
那完全就是另一码事了。
if you try to trade one in,
it's a different story.

209
00:11:45,640 --> 00:11:47,640
这种车只要开上六个月，
The story of these cars
going six months old,

210
00:11:47,680 --> 00:11:49,320
身价就直接暴跌五万英镑。
with, like, 50 grand depreciation.

211
00:11:49,360 --> 00:11:51,440
新车17万，二手就只剩12万了。
So 170 new, 120 secondhhand.

212
00:11:51,480 --> 00:11:56,120
所以归根结底，从投资保值的角度来说，
法拉利完胜。
So basically, then, the Ferrari is a
winner as far as an investment's concerned.

213
00:11:56,160 --> 00:11:59,560
在公路上它也是赢家。
但要是上了赛道呢？
It's a winner on the road.
But, what about on the track?

214
00:12:00,120 --> 00:12:04,420
按说赛道成绩也该毫无悬念才对，
但斯提格刚给自己买了
It should be a foregone conclusion here
too, but The Stig had just bought himself

