00:12:04,440 --> 00:12:07,740
一张Boston乐队的新CD，正琢磨着放来听听。
♪ Boston - More Than A Feeling ♪
a new Boston CD, and he
wanted to give it a spin.
♪ Boston - More Than A Feeling ♪

216
00:12:09,200 --> 00:12:12,400
于是，我们显然得先放他开着
那台阿斯顿·马丁出去撒欢。
So, we let him loose obviously
in the Aston Martin first of all.

217
00:12:12,900 --> 00:12:18,700
他冲过来了……最后一个小分段，
过完木匠弯（Carpenters Corner）之后
Here he comes now... last little section,
coming across the line after Carpenters

218
00:12:18,720 --> 00:12:20,540
准备冲线。
Corner here.

219
00:12:20,560 --> 00:12:25,080
克拉克森：成绩是1分
36秒。
CLARKSON: And it's one minute,
thirty-six seconds.

220
00:12:26,160 --> 00:12:30,840
现在，换上法拉利，
车里依旧放着他的Boston CD。
Now, into the Ferrari,
with his Boston CD again.

221
00:12:30,880 --> 00:12:31,760
♪ Boston - More Than A Feeling ♪
♪ Boston - More Than A Feeling ♪

222
00:12:34,440 --> 00:12:37,760
克拉克森：目标是击败
1分36秒。
这是最后一个弯角了。
CLARKSON: One minute,
thirty-six to beat.
The final corner here.

223
00:12:37,800 --> 00:12:41,040
他能做到吗？
1分36秒，然后……
Is he going to do it?
1:36, and...

224
00:12:41,080 --> 00:12:44,560
不出所料，确实比阿斯顿更快，
对吧？
Predictably, it is quicker
than the Aston, okay?

225
00:12:44,600 --> 00:12:47,440
但神奇的是，居然只快了整整一秒！
But, and this is amazing, by one second

226
00:12:47,480 --> 00:12:49,400
就快这么点？
- 最终成绩是1分35秒。
Is that all?
- The time is 1:35.

227
00:12:49,440 --> 00:12:50,520
现在我来把它贴到圈速榜上。
Now I am going to put that on the board.

228
00:12:50,560 --> 00:12:53,400
两台车都在这儿了，排在Noble后面。
There they both are, behind the Noble.

229
00:12:53,440 --> 00:12:57,560
但别忘了，当时可是……
我特意在代表湿地的“W”下画了线，就是这么湿。
But remember, it was...
I've underlined W for wet. It was that wet

230
00:12:57,600 --> 00:12:59,520
当时外面的路况简直糟透了。
It really was horrendous out there.

231
00:12:59,560 --> 00:13:00,880
不过可别以为这能难倒斯提格。
Don't think that put The Stig off, though.

232
00:13:00,920 --> 00:13:02,600
他真的是豁出去了，因为接着就发生了这一幕。
He really tried because this happened.

233
00:13:04,960 --> 00:13:08,320
克拉克森：以大约140英里的时速
切入这个弯道。
CLARKSON: About 140 miles
an hour through this corner.

234
00:13:08,360 --> 00:13:10,840
[轮胎尖叫声]
[TYRES SCREECHING]

235
00:13:10,880 --> 00:13:12,480
[笑声]
[LAUGHTER]

236
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:18,240
那么开车可不算勇敢，
纯粹就是脑子有坑。
That's not bravery, doing that.
That's just stupidity.

237
00:13:18,280 --> 00:13:21,840
好了，我们今晚稍微带了点
一级方程式的主题，
Now, we've got a bit of
a Formula One theme going on tonight

238
00:13:21,880 --> 00:13:25,400
这也是为什么这玩意儿
会出现在我们的小天地里。
which is why this has come
into our little world.

239
00:13:25,440 --> 00:13:29,320
你看，F1车队成天跟我们吹嘘，
说他们赛车上的高科技和精巧技术，
You see, Formula One teams are forever
telling us that the technology and gizmos

240
00:13:29,360 --> 00:13:34,920
迟早都会下放到
你我平时买的家用车上。
on their cars, eventually filter down
to the cars that you and I buy every day.

241
00:13:34,960 --> 00:13:37,960
照这么说，
咱们现在开上街的，
Well, on that basis,
we'd all be driving around now

242
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:41,600
可全是埃尔顿·塞纳开过的那种1988款迈凯伦了，
in a 1998 McLaren as driven by Ayrton Senna

243
00:13:41,640 --> 00:13:43,000
但显然，咱们并没有。
and, of course, we're not.

244
00:13:43,040 --> 00:13:46,400
事实上，我唯一能想到
In fact, the only technology I can think of

245
00:13:46,440 --> 00:13:48,560
一级方程式赛车带给我们的民用技术，
that Formula One has given us

246
00:13:48,600 --> 00:13:51,800
也就是那种蠢得要死的变速箱，
反正根本没人稀罕。
are those stupid gearboxes
that we don't want anyway.

247
00:13:51,840 --> 00:13:55,080
不过拉力赛，那可就完全是另一码事了。
Now, rallying, that's
a completely different animal.

248
00:13:55,120 --> 00:13:59,680
没错，它起码还给英语词典
贡献了一个词呢。
Sure. It has contributed one
word to the English language.

249
00:13:59,720 --> 00:14:03,040
有人想斗胆猜猜
会是哪个词吗？
Does anybody want to hazard
a guess what that word might be?

250
00:14:03,080 --> 00:14:04,760
男观众：冲锋衣。
MAN: Anorak.

251
00:14:04,800 --> 00:14:07,360
冲锋衣。这位先生您懂的，您太懂了。
[全场大笑]
Anorak. You'd know, sir. You'd know.
[ALL LAUGHING]

252
00:14:07,400 --> 00:14:09,480
完全正确。这可不是什么爱斯基摩词汇，
Absolutely right. It's not an Eskimo word.

253
00:14:09,520 --> 00:14:13,800
而是指大家坐在威尔士山坡上
淋着雨看比赛时穿的那种衣服。
It's what people wear on
the Welsh hillsides when they
are sitting in the rain.

254
00:14:13,840 --> 00:14:16,560
不过，拉力赛带给我们的，
可远不止这些。
But, rallying has given us
quite a lot more,

255
00:14:16,600 --> 00:14:19,280
除了冲锋衣，还有涡轮增压、四轮驱动。
besides. Turbo charging. Four-wheel Drive.

256
00:14:19,320 --> 00:14:23,320
要是你走进宝马展厅问：“我能买这台赛车吗？”
And, if you walked into
a BMW showroom and said "Can I buy this,"

257
00:14:23,360 --> 00:14:26,680
他们肯定会说：“不行，买不了。”
they'd say, "No. You can't."

258
00:14:26,720 --> 00:14:30,200
但你却能买到三菱Evo七代，
But, you can buy a Mitsubishi Evo VII.

259
00:14:30,240 --> 00:14:32,400
你能买到斯巴鲁翼豹，
You can buy a Subaru Impreza.

260
00:14:32,440 --> 00:14:34,400
而且这种传统早已有之。
And this has been going on for ages.

261
00:14:34,440 --> 00:14:38,400
你当年能买到奥迪Quattro、
福特Escort Cosworth，或者蓝旗亚Delta Integrale。
You could buy an Audi Quattro
or an Escort Cosworth or a Delta Integrale.

262
00:14:38,440 --> 00:14:40,640
拉力赛把货真价实的好车带给了我们。
Rallying gives us the cars.

263
00:14:40,680 --> 00:14:43,880
而且它还带给了我们另一样东西：一位世界冠军。
And there's something else
it gives us, a World Champion.

264
00:14:43,920 --> 00:14:46,840
他今天就在现场！女士们先生们，
理查德·伯恩斯！
And he's here. Ladies
and Gentlemen, Richard Burns!

265
00:14:46,880 --> 00:14:48,280
[全场欢呼]
[ALL CHEERING]

266
00:14:49,360 --> 00:14:51,560
最近怎么样，理查德？
- 挺好的。
How are you, Richard?
- Good.

267
00:14:54,000 --> 00:14:56,840
那么他们打算拿一级方程式怎么办呢？
So what are they going to do
about Formula One?

268
00:14:56,880 --> 00:14:58,800
呃，尽量让它变得更有趣点吧。
Erm, try to make it more interesting.

269
00:14:58,840 --> 00:15:01,480
尽量让它变得跟拉力赛一样精彩。
Try to make it as interesting as Rallying.

270
00:15:01,520 --> 00:15:02,922
可不就是嘛，你要知道，
拉力赛以前总被当成
Well, that's it, you know,
'cause Rallying is always seen

271
00:15:02,947 --> 00:15:03,720
不受待见的“穷亲戚”，不是吗？
as the poor relation, isn't it?

272
00:15:03,760 --> 00:15:06,520
但说实话，它现在办得相当出彩了。
But actually, it's coming quite good now.

273
00:15:06,560 --> 00:15:08,720
我觉得确实。现在参赛的汽车厂商更多了，
I think it is. There is
more manufacturers in it.

274
00:15:08,760 --> 00:15:11,015
现在真正有实力赢下拉力分站赛的人，
There's a lot more people
who can actually win a rally now

275
00:15:11,040 --> 00:15:12,200
可比一级方程式里多得多。
than there is in Formula One.

276
00:15:12,240 --> 00:15:14,600
而且我只是……我希望那些……
And I just... I hope that some of
the people who are...

277
00:15:14,640 --> 00:15:16,720
弃看F1的人，能转过来看咱们拉力赛。
Stopped watching that are
going to start watching this.

278
00:15:16,760 --> 00:15:18,960
没错，确实。不过说实话，拉力赛对你可真不薄。
Yeah, that true. It's been kind
to you, let's be honest.

279
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:22,160
咱们实话实说嘛。
- 我这周看了两份报纸，
Let's be honest.
- I was seeing two papers this week.

280
00:15:22,200 --> 00:15:24,920
你现在的收入可是简森·巴顿的两倍呢。
Twice as much you're earning
now as Jenson Button.

281
00:15:24,960 --> 00:15:27,440
噢，真的吗？那我年纪
可足足是他的两倍呢。
Oh, really? Well, I'm twice
as old as he is.

282
00:15:27,480 --> 00:15:28,800
克拉克森：没错。
[全场笑声]
CLARKSON: Yes.
[LAUGHTER]

283
00:15:28,840 --> 00:15:31,200
而且你还是个避税逃港客。
- 确实是。
And you're a tax exile.
- I am.

284
00:15:31,240 --> 00:15:33,160
在安道尔买了房。
- 没错。
Got a house in Andorra.
- I have.

285
00:15:33,200 --> 00:15:36,080
还找了个女朋友。
- 对，这显而易见
很费银子。
Got a girlfriend.
- Yeah, which you need
money for. Obviously.

286
00:15:36,120 --> 00:15:38,440
[全场大笑]
- 没错。而且你居然还顶着一头红发。
[ALL LAUGHING]
- Yes. And you've still got ginger hair.

287
00:15:38,480 --> 00:15:39,960
在发型上你可是一分钱都没舍得花。
You haven't spent any money there.

288
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:41,920
哎，话是这么说，但我好歹剪掉大半了。
- 这倒是。
Yeah, well, I did cut most of it off.
- Yeah.

289
00:15:41,960 --> 00:15:43,920
你开车干嘛总单手打方向？
这我实在琢磨不透。
Why do you drive one-handed?
That's what I can't understand.

290
00:15:43,960 --> 00:15:46,000
看着就跟完全没认真开似的。
It looks like you're really not trying.

291
00:15:46,040 --> 00:15:48,440
我是说，哥们儿，双手握把轮子好吗，
那样你还能开得更快点。
I mean, put both hands
on the wheel, man. You'll go faster.

292
00:15:48,480 --> 00:15:50,280
有动力转向嘛，单手轻松得很。
Got power steering. It's easy.

293
00:15:50,320 --> 00:15:52,720
可你到底图啥？你每次开
都只把一只手搭在方向盘上。
But why do you do it? You've always
just got one hand on the wheel.

294
00:15:52,760 --> 00:15:55,640
以前是这样，但现在换挡拨片
都在方向盘上了，所以就……
I used to but now you've got the gear
change on the wheel then it's like...

295
00:15:55,680 --> 00:15:57,840
噢，别告诉我你车上也装了那玩意儿？
- 抱歉，还真装了。
Oh, you haven't got that as well, have you?
- Sorry.

296
00:15:57,880 --> 00:16:00,840
[全场大笑]
- 那玩意儿纯属垃圾，根本不好使。
[ALL LAUGHING]
- It's rubbish, it doesn't work.

297
00:16:00,880 --> 00:16:03,160
对我挺好使的。
- 所以你才丢了年度总冠军啊。
It does with me.
- That's why you've lost the championship.

298
00:16:03,200 --> 00:16:06,240
全赖你那变速箱。
不过说正经的，你到底怎么丢的冠？
Because of your gearbox.
Actually, no, why have you lost it?

299
00:16:06,280 --> 00:16:08,200
呃，我们这一整年表现平平，
Um, we've had a fairly average year

300
00:16:08,240 --> 00:16:10,680
而咱队友却开挂般惊艳。
说白了，就这么回事。
and our teammate has had a spectacular one.
Simple as that, really.

301
00:16:10,720 --> 00:16:13,120
“我们”？不，表现平平的只有你。
- 我和罗伯特（里德）啊。
We. No, you have.
- Me and Robert (Reid).

302
00:16:13,160 --> 00:16:14,640
我们是一个团队。
- 噢，你们当然是一个团队了。
We're a team.
- Oh, of course you are a team.

303
00:16:14,680 --> 00:16:15,840
我都得听他的。
- 没错，正是如此。
I have to listen to him.
- Yeah, exactly.

304
00:16:15,880 --> 00:16:18,400
而且还是他害你
狠狠撞了个大翻车，对吧？
And he caused you to have
a good crash, didn't he?

305
00:16:18,440 --> 00:16:19,880
那次完完全全是他的锅，没错。
That was totally his fault. Yeah.

306
00:16:19,920 --> 00:16:21,400
[全场大笑]
[ALL LAUGHING]

307
00:16:21,440 --> 00:16:25,160
几周前我在新西兰
出了次相当严重的事故。
I had a quite big accident
a few weeks ago, in New Zealand.

308
00:16:25,200 --> 00:16:27,240
呃，那次倒全是我自己的责任。
Erm, when it was totally my fault.

309
00:16:27,280 --> 00:16:29,080
车速没毛病，
但弯道实在太急了。
The speed was right,
but the corner was too tight.

310
00:16:29,120 --> 00:16:32,560
你年轻的时候，
并不喜欢去酒吧和蹦迪，
When you were younger,
you didn't like going to pubs and discos,

311
00:16:32,600 --> 00:16:34,840
反倒更乐意跟拉力圈的人混在一起。
and you preferred the company
of Rally people.

312
00:16:34,880 --> 00:16:36,160
是啊，不过后来我长大了，
Yeah, but then I grew up,

313
00:16:36,200 --> 00:16:38,600
手里也有了你刚才提到的那些闲钱，
and I had that money
you were talking about,

314
00:16:38,640 --> 00:16:40,560
这才领会到夜生活有多爽。
and found out what all that was about.

315
00:16:40,600 --> 00:16:42,920
所以现在我确实常泡酒吧。
So now I do go to the pub.

316
00:16:42,960 --> 00:16:46,240
坦白讲，我觉得如果你不让自己
过点稍微正常人的日子，
To be honest, I think if you don't allow
yourself to live a slightly normal life,

317
00:16:46,280 --> 00:16:48,480
我猜要不了多久你就会想一枪崩了自己。
you're going to want to shoot yourself
fairly quickly, I would think.

318
00:16:48,520 --> 00:16:51,520
可不是嘛！我是说，前几天我还看到
你最大的宿敌科林·麦克雷的照片，
Well exactly. I mean, I saw
a picture of your great rival
Colin McRae the other day

319
00:16:51,560 --> 00:16:55,680
居然在比赛期间
大口猛炫咖喱酱配薯条。
tucking in on a race to
a curry sauce and chips.

320
00:16:55,720 --> 00:16:57,920
讲真，我可从没见过
哪个F1车手会……
Now, I've never seen
a Formula One driver going,

321
00:16:57,960 --> 00:17:00,000
“给我上面浇点咖喱酱。”
"I'll have the curry sauce on that."

322
00:17:00,040 --> 00:17:01,880
他们的品味可没那么高雅。
They are not cultured enough.

323
00:17:01,920 --> 00:17:05,320
不管怎么说，当然了，
现在是那个……叫什么来着？
Anyway, of course,
it's the, erm... what's it called now?

324
00:17:05,360 --> 00:17:07,680
异口同声：Network Q英国拉力赛。
BOTH: Network Q Rally GB.

325
00:17:07,720 --> 00:17:09,920
克拉克森：……下周开——
呃，是这周晚些时候开赛，对吧？
CLARKSON: ...starts next,
well, later this week, isn't it?

326
00:17:09,960 --> 00:17:11,200
对。
- 星期几？
Yeah.
- What day is it?

327
00:17:11,240 --> 00:17:13,240
周五开赛，没错。
- 周五，好的。
Starts on Friday. Yeah.
- Friday. Okay.

328
00:17:13,280 --> 00:17:16,360
而且你拿过三次冠军。
- 三次。
And you've won that three times.
- Three times.

329
00:17:16,400 --> 00:17:18,120
功课做得很足嘛。
You've done your research.

330
00:17:18,160 --> 00:17:19,880
你坐在车里，车里有暖风，
对吧？
You sit in the car, you've got a heater,
haven't you?

331
00:17:19,920 --> 00:17:22,400
我们是有暖风。
- 所以你舒服得很嘛。
We've got a heater.
- So you are quite comfortable.

332
00:17:22,440 --> 00:17:25,640
那你有没有想过，
那会是什么滋味……跟我来。
Have you ever thought,
what would it be like... come with me.

333
00:17:25,680 --> 00:17:27,600
你有没有想过那究竟是什么滋味，
Have you ever thought what would it be like

334
00:17:27,640 --> 00:17:31,280
对那些大老远跑去现场
看拉力赛的观众来说？
for the people who have
to turn up and spectate on the rally?

335
00:17:31,320 --> 00:17:33,200
我记得，我以前干过……我以前也是观众。
I remember, I did... I used to do that.

336
00:17:33,240 --> 00:17:35,440
你去过？
- 去过啊。
You did?
- Yeah.

337
00:17:35,480 --> 00:17:37,800
好吧，我看你脑子里早把那罪受成啥样给忘光了。
Well, I'm not sure whether you have really
got it at the forefront of your head.

338
00:17:37,840 --> 00:17:41,440
所以我想让你重新感受一把
当拉力赛现场观众的滋味，行吗？
So I want to give you a flavour
of what it is to be like to be
a rally spectator, okay?

339
00:17:41,480 --> 00:17:43,640
那就麻烦你站到外面去吧。多谢合作。
So if you would just like
to step out there. Thanks very much.

340
00:17:44,280 --> 00:17:45,680
[全场大笑]
[ALL LAUGHING]

341
00:17:45,720 --> 00:17:47,480
好啦，呃……
[全场鼓掌]
Right, um...
[ALL APPLAUDING]

342
00:17:51,360 --> 00:17:53,840
现在，我们就把他晾在外面，
Now, we'll leave him out there

343
00:17:53,880 --> 00:17:57,440
直到他整颗脑袋都被冻得发青。
until his whole head's turned blue.

344
00:17:57,480 --> 00:18:01,440
那么，要是有一辆车跟F1一级方程式
八竿子打不着，
What about a car that's got
nothing to do with Formula One,

345
00:18:01,480 --> 00:18:03,480
跟拉力赛也毫无瓜葛呢？
and nothing to do with Rallying?

346
00:18:03,520 --> 00:18:05,440
日产Skyline。
The Nissan Skyline.

347
00:18:05,480 --> 00:18:09,920
它基本上就是一台屁股上插了根排气管的
巨型PlayStation。
It's basically a huge PlayStation, with
an exhaust pipe on the back.

348
00:18:09,960 --> 00:18:11,960
如果你有兴趣
淘一辆二手货，
And if you're interested
in buying a secondhand one,

349
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:13,720
有几件事你必须先弄清楚。
there's a few things you need to know.

350
00:18:16,800 --> 00:18:19,040
在世界超跑的荣誉榜上，
In the world league table of supercars,

351
00:18:19,080 --> 00:18:23,560
日本真正拿得出手的贡献只有这一个：
日产Skyline。
（难道是NSX？）
Japan has only made one real contribution,
the Nissan Skyline.
(NSX?)

352
00:18:23,600 --> 00:18:28,200
它或许没有阿斯顿·马丁或法拉利那种
性感尤物的身段与纯正贵族血统，
It may not have the looks and the pedigree
of an Aston Martin or Ferrari,

353
00:18:28,240 --> 00:18:31,200
但话说回来，它的身价也从来没那么高高在上。
but then again, it never had
the price tag, either.

354
00:18:32,480 --> 00:18:34,080
可它的狂暴速度绝对货真价实。
But it certainly had the pace.

355
00:18:37,840 --> 00:18:40,880
无论它去哪儿参赛，
都能把对手按在地上疯狂碾压。
Wherever it went racing,
it crushed the opposition.

356
00:18:40,920 --> 00:18:43,680
事实上，在澳大利亚房车锦标赛中，
In fact, in the Australian
Touring Car series

357
00:18:43,720 --> 00:18:47,000
主办方甚至不惜修改规则，
就为了名正言顺地把它彻底禁赛。
they changed the rules
so the car could be outlawed.

358
00:18:47,040 --> 00:18:49,640
Skyline真正的杀手锏全藏在车壳之下：
The Skyline's strength lies under the skin

359
00:18:49,680 --> 00:18:52,960
揭开机盖，你会看到一台276匹制动马力、
where you'll find a 276-brake horsepower,

360
00:18:53,000 --> 00:18:57,360
双涡轮增压发动机，以及一副令人叹为观止的
电脑控制底盘。
twin turbo, and an incredible
computer-controlled chassis

361
00:18:57,400 --> 00:18:59,600
你想耍帅时它就是两驱，
that can be two-wheel drive
when you want it

362
00:18:59,640 --> 00:19:01,560
需要救命时又能瞬间切成四驱。
and four-wheel drive when you need it.

363
00:19:03,480 --> 00:19:05,720
但这台“科技巨兽”的好日子到头了，
But it's all over for this Techno titan

364
00:19:05,760 --> 00:19:08,280
因为就在今年，
他们把Skyline停产了。
because this year
they stopped building Skylines.

365
00:19:08,320 --> 00:19:13,200
这台来自日本的平民超跑，
如今你只能在二手车市场淘了。
And Japan's cut-price supercar
is now available only as a secondhand buy.

366
00:19:15,480 --> 00:19:17,720
总共有三代车型
可供挑选：
In all, there were three models
to choose from,

367
00:19:17,760 --> 00:19:21,560
90年代前半叶生产的R32，
（其实是89到94年）
the R32 which was built
in the first half of the '90s,
('89 - '94)

368
00:19:21,600 --> 00:19:25,440
活跃在96到99年的R33，
（其实是95到98年）
the R33 which comes around
from '96 to '99,
('95 - '98)

369
00:19:25,480 --> 00:19:29,240
最后，就是名字起得极其“富有想象力”的R34。
and finally, the imaginatively-named R34.

370
00:19:29,280 --> 00:19:32,480
零到六十英里加速只要5.2秒，
Which, with a 0 to 60 time of 5.2 seconds,

371
00:19:32,520 --> 00:19:37,080
极速可达每小时155英里，
堪称全系巅峰之作。
（其实它们全都能跑155）
and a top speed of 155 miles per hour,
was the best of the breed.
(They all "did" 155)

372
00:19:39,160 --> 00:19:41,760
噢！[大笑]
Oh! [LAUGHING]

373
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:44,560
[呼气] 太过瘾了。
[EXHALES] That was nice.

374
00:19:47,640 --> 00:19:49,600
它不仅快得让人头皮发麻，
Not only is it blisteringly quick,

375
00:19:49,640 --> 00:19:51,840
而且开起来简直是“傻瓜级”的难度，
but it's almost idiot-proof to drive

376
00:19:51,880 --> 00:19:56,120
那套全电脑控制的底盘，甚至能把
笨手笨脚的莫琳大妈调教成迈克尔·舒马赫。
with that computerised chassis capable of
turning Maureen into Michael Schumacher.

377
00:19:56,160 --> 00:19:59,600
极其聪明的扭矩分配系统，
还有主动偏航控制。
A really clever tool converter,
you've got active dual control.

378
00:19:59,640 --> 00:20:01,480
各个车轮上都布满了传感器，
There are sensors all around on the wheels

379
00:20:01,520 --> 00:20:04,760
还有陀螺仪时刻汇报
你的过弯速度和加速度。
and gyroscopes telling how fast you
are cornering and accelerating.

380
00:20:04,800 --> 00:20:08,920
它们把所有这些数据一股脑丢进
一个16位处理器里，
They chuck all that information
into a 16-bit processor

381
00:20:08,960 --> 00:20:11,560
结果就是，这台车
等于在全程护着你。
and the outcome is, the car
kind of looks after you.

382
00:20:11,600 --> 00:20:13,600
过起弯来那叫一个快得离谱。
It doesn't half make a corner quick.

383
00:20:17,080 --> 00:20:19,760
再看看这块显示屏？
瞧瞧这个，哦吼！
What about the display here?
Look at this. Ooh!

384
00:20:20,840 --> 00:20:22,280
一边开着车，
As we drive along,

385
00:20:22,320 --> 00:20:25,680
我们一边能看自己过弯时吃了多少G值。
we can check how many G
we are going round corners.

386
00:20:25,720 --> 00:20:29,400
还能查看……呃，涡轮增压值。
We can check the, er, turbo boost.

387
00:20:29,440 --> 00:20:32,720
还能看前轮分配到了多少扭矩。
We can check the torque
to the front wheels.

388
00:20:32,760 --> 00:20:36,800
我是说，这玩意儿能让你
沉迷上……足足好几分钟呢！
I mean, it is going to keep you
occupied for, what... minutes!

389
00:20:41,560 --> 00:20:43,800
真是个绝妙的尤物。
Fantastic bit of kit.

390
00:20:43,840 --> 00:20:49,080
这绝对是一台为
“PS游戏机世代”量身打造的车。
It really is a car for
the PlayStation generation.

391
00:20:56,040 --> 00:20:59,040
我是它的狂热铁粉。
显而易见我们都是，确实是台好车。
Big fan of the car.
We all are, obviously, great car.

392
00:20:59,080 --> 00:21:01,000
那你究竟该买哪一款？
Which one should you buy?

393
00:21:01,040 --> 00:21:03,000
关于Skyline，你首先得明白的一点
Well, the first thing you've got to realise
about the Skylines

394
00:21:03,040 --> 00:21:05,400
就是买它的人，基本都是当大玩具使的。
is that, they're mainly
bought as playthings.

395
00:21:05,440 --> 00:21:08,760
所以你去看车时，经常能碰上里程很低、
So if you get on looking at one,
you can find a car with quite low mileage

396
00:21:08,800 --> 00:21:10,600
但过户记录却有三四手的车。
that's got, like, three or four
owners on it.

